About the Power BI dashboard:

Adventure Works: Operations Dashboard – Sales & Inventory Trends

This dashboard is build to keep track and to make sure any issues with Inventory, Sales and a more detailed overview of our Products performance There are filters that can help further help get more detailed information in every page:

Date: Selectable by Year and/or Month, and each page gets filter for that specific time period
Region: for this project it is set to US
Inventory Category
Online v Offline: Sales and Product Performance pages will use this filter the most to find key diffrences between Online and Offline sales
Contents of the dashboard:

Overview
Sales
Product Performance
Inventory
Overview

Gives a quick overview of the companies Sales and Product performance and the most important KPIs from May 2011 to June 2014, as well as key elements to show Inventories situation All of the elements on this page are also present on all of the other pages for detailed view, overview page is more of a way to quickly glance at the key results.

Sales

Contains most important KPIs in terms of sales, like: Order Volume, Total Revenue, Average Order Value, Year-over-Year growth and Year-to-Date Revenue for the company Also, include a Total Revenue and Order Volume grapgh to show changes over time and a table for Online and Offline order to highlight the key diffrences

Product Performance

Contains Product related KPIs, such as Top 5 Products, Top 5 Subcategories that generated the most revenue and Items Sold by Category The graph at the bottom contains information about the volume of products sold and manufactured, as well as a line showing stock turnover %, highlighting the fluctuations of our stock

Inventory

Showcases the current inventory stock, safe levels of each individual Product and has conditional formating to highlight stock that is below safe levels (not affected by the date filter as it shows stock that is in the warehouse, stocked and ready to be sold) Also, contains another tables to showcase each individual products performance: Items Sold, Manufactured and the Stock Turnover for each product separetly, here we can track which products are sold and which one of them has the most turnover rate
